    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d20">

                <pb facs="0125" n="94" xml:id="pg94"/>

                <head>20. Message From President Nixon to Japanese Prime Minister Tanaka<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d20-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1973-03-03">March 3, 1973</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Dear Mr. Prime Minister:</p>
                <p>I have today received a letter from Chancellor Brandt informing me that the
                    European countries are planning to develop a proposal to deal with the current
                    currency crisis.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d20-f2"/> I want you to know that I have
                    replied to Chancellor Brandt and have also written to Prime Minister Heath
                    saying that any solution to the currency crisis should be developed through full
                    consultations with the United States and with Japan<anchor n="3" xml:id="d20-f3"
                    />—a point we had previously made orally to Prime Minister Heath.</p>
                <p>We will be prepared to exchange views with you on this subject.</p>
                <p>With kind regards.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Richard Nixon</hi>
                    </signed><anchor n="4" xml:id="d20-f4"/>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
